The errors in the test code were caused by type mismatches between `uint256` and `uint8` when handling the number of player cards. Since the Blackjack game has a limited deck size (52 cards), we can safely cast the card numbers to `uint8` without risking overflow. The fixes include:

1. Added explicit casting of `getPlayerCardsNumber()` return value to `uint8` since the maximum cards per hand (52) fits in uint8
2. Added casting of loop indices to `uint8` when calling `getPlayerCard()`
3. Added casting when indexing the last card after the "hit" operation
4. Retained all logging and vulnerability verification logic

